            "reviewBody": "This is the same recipe that I've been making for years and the same one that my mom has been making.",
            "datePublished": "2026-05-10T17:28:06.468Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good, but doubled the amount of miracle whip and it was perfect.",
            "datePublished": "2026-04-06T03:31:07.317Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Bruce Carlton Kitchen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made these deviled eggs and taking them to a family holiday event tonight, I chose this recipe for two reasons: the directions and number of ingredients were my ideal preference, and so many deviled egg recipes include relish - which may taste ok with something cooked on a grill made from lips, but not eggs. Thank you, Mary, for no relish! My family will give me their official reviews later, but the two i've sampled were terrific.",
            "datePublished": "2025-12-23T10:54:23.564Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "zerodramamama"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe tastes great (use your eyeballs to judge the consistency of the deviled mixture)! PREP time is WAY OFF. It takes 10 minutes to bring eggs in water to a boil. Remove from heat, COVER, and let stand for at least 15 minutes (I go 20-30). Then drain and soak in ice bath (10 minutes, at least, overnight works best). I use 12 eggs, so it takes about 1/2 hour to peel them CAREFULLY under running cold water. The rest takes less than 1/2 hour (cut/mix-I use white pepper for a cleaner lookfill-a baby feeding spoon works GREAT!). I never used Miracle Whip before, but I like the flavors, and I'm waiting for the family reviews tomorrow.",
            "datePublished": "2025-11-26T13:47:27.943Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "tagurit58"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I doubled the amount of mayo. I didn't use Miracle Whip, although that's how my mother showed me using MW in place of mayo. I don't like it too sweet I could have added a bit of sweet pickle juice to give it a tiny bit of sweetness but not too much. I used Turmeric in place of Paprika because I was out. It's a good sub and good for us.",
            "datePublished": "2024-10-15T17:09:18.577Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mindy Knight"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved this easy recipe. The only thing I do differently is I add sweet pickle relish. Yum!",
            "datePublished": "2024-02-21T17:51:18.021Z"
          }
